{"format":1,"key":"zone:thunderbluff","path":"/lore/zone/thunderbluff","name":"Thunder Bluff","kind":"zone","label":"Capital","zone":{"key":"thunderbluff","name":"Thunder Bluff","path":"/lore/zone/thunderbluff"},"levels":"","description":"Across the plains of Mulgore, Thunder Bluff shelters the tauren above the grasslands. High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof founded the city after uniting the…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:thunderbluff","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Across the plains of Mulgore, Thunder Bluff shelters the tauren above the grasslands. High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof founded the city after uniting the nomadic tribes with the New Horde. Rope bridges and wooden lifts link its mesas, while its heights offer safety from centaur marauders and shelter travelers crossing Kalimdor.","For generations, the tauren wandered across Kalimdor, struggling to survive centaur attacks. During the Third War, Cairne Bloodhoof joined Warchief Thrall, and together the orcs and tauren drove back the centaur and secured Mulgore’s pastures. Cairne led the allied tribes to these natural stone heights to guard their future. Thunder Bluff became their first unified, permanent home in centuries.","Thunder Bluff stretches across high mesas, joined by rope bridges. The central bluffs hold the markets, bank, inn, and Wind Rider roost. Three more mesas rise beyond them. Hunter Rise serves scouts and trackers. Elder Rise is home to lorekeepers and the Cenarion Circle, led by Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. Spirit Rise is devoted to spiritual communion, with shelter for shamans and priests and the underground Pools of Vision."],"hash":"f64146","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"070c8b3350","sec":69},"female-narrator":{"sha":"f42a2b5dd1","sec":76}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Thunder Bluff","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Thunder_Bluff"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/npc/cairne-bloodhoof","n":"Cairne Bloodhoof","k":"npc"},{"p":"/lore/zone/mulgore","n